\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The saturation is largely a preprocessing artefact, not an intrinsic property of the estimator.}{11}{section*.9}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The criterion is dominated by redundancy and is estimator-saturated. (a) Distribution of $\Psi ^{(1)}$ per 60\,s window by macro feature (box: quartiles, whiskers: 5th--95th percentile, annotation: median, right column: percentage of windows with $\Psi >0$). $|\Psi |$ is largest, and positive range scarcest, for the linear aggregates, the two non-linear clustering coefficients are the only features with usable headroom. The grey line marks the saturation floor at $-23.1$ nats. (b) $\Psi $ against the negated micro sum for \texttt  {\small  V\_all} (6{,}000-window sample), $r=0.995$. The vertical offset from the identity line is $I(V_t;V_{t'})$, the entire macro contribution. (c) Distribution of the per-player term $I(X^i_t;V_{t'})$ for the linear features: $24\,\%$ of terms sit at the estimator's ceiling of $2.57$ nats at $N\approx 59$, $k=4$. Note that $88.6\,\%$ of that saturation falls inside the clock-artefact void described in the text; outside it the figure is $3.8\,\%$.\relax }}{12}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:floor}{{1}{12}{The criterion is dominated by redundancy and is estimator-saturated. (a) Distribution of $\Psi ^{(1)}$ per 60\,s window by macro feature (box: quartiles, whiskers: 5th--95th percentile, annotation: median, right column: percentage of windows with $\Psi >0$). $|\Psi |$ is largest, and positive range scarcest, for the linear aggregates, the two non-linear clustering coefficients are the only features with usable headroom. The grey line marks the saturation floor at $-23.1$ nats. (b) $\Psi $ against the negated micro sum for \code {V\_all} (6{,}000-window sample), $r=0.995$. The vertical offset from the identity line is $I(V_t;V_{t'})$, the entire macro contribution. (c) Distribution of the per-player term $I(X^i_t;V_{t'})$ for the linear features: $24\,\%$ of terms sit at the estimator's ceiling of $2.57$ nats at $N\approx 59$, $k=4$. Note that $88.6\,\%$ of that saturation falls inside the clock-artefact void described in the text; outside it the figure is $3.8\,\%$.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:floor@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][11][]12}}
